 sure `node --test` run from `packages/jsonl-lint` finds them (files in `test/` named `*.test.js`).\n5. Write `packages/jsonl-lint/README.md`: what it does, usage (`node packages/jsonl-lint/bin/jsonl-lint.js <file>`), output format, exit codes 0/1/2, and the `lint(text)` API.\n6. Update the root `README.md`: replace the \"No tools yet\" line with a list of tools that includes `packages/jsonl-lint` with a one-line description.\n7. Run `npm install` at the root to update `package-lock.json` for the new workspace, then `npm ci && npm test` at the root and confirm it passes and the jsonl-lint tests actually ran. Also try the CLI by hand on a clean, bad, missing and no-argument case.\n8. Commit, push and open one PR to the repository whose body contains the line `Closes https://github.com/suredesigntshirts/ccp_machine_test/issues/102`. Wait for the `test` workflow on the PR head to finish; if it fails, fix and push until it is green.","verifier":"Check out the PR head of the single PR for issue https://github.com/suredesigntshirts/ccp_machine_test/issues/102 on suredesigntshirts/ccp_machine_test. Run `npm ci` at the repository root first. Make test files in a fresh temp dir (`T=$(mktemp -d)`). One check per expect line, in order.\n\n### Check 1 — expect: \"packages/jsonl-lint/bin/jsonl-lint.js <file> prints <file>:<line>: <error> for every row that is not valid JSON (1-based lines, blank lines skipped, an unterminated last line checked) and exits 1 if any, 0 if none\"\nRun:\n- `printf '{\"a\":1}\\n[2]\\n\"x\"\\n' > $T/clean.jsonl; node packages/jsonl-lint/bin/jsonl-lint.js $T/clean.jsonl; echo \"exit=$?\"`\n- `printf '{\"a\":1}\\nnot json\\n{\"b\":2}\\n' > $T/mid.jsonl; node packages/jsonl-lint/bin/jsonl-lint.js $T/mid.jsonl; echo \"exit=$?\"`\n- `printf '{\"a\":1}\\n\\n   \\n{bad\\n{\"c\":3}\\n{\"d\":' > $T/mix.jsonl; node packages/jsonl-lint/bin/jsonl-lint.js $T/mix.jsonl; echo \"exit=$?\"`\n- `printf '\\n\\n{\"a\":1}\\n\\n' > $T/blank.jsonl; node packages/jsonl-lint/bin/jsonl-lint.js $T/blank.jsonl; echo \"exit=$?\"`\nPASS: clean.jsonl exits 0 with no error lines; mid.jsonl exits 1 and prints exactly one error line starting `$T/mid.jsonl:2: ` followed by a non-empty message; mix.jsonl exits 1 and prints exactly two error lines, starting `$T/mix.jsonl:4: ` and `$T/mix.jsonl:6: ` (blank lines 2 and 3 not reported, unterminated last line 6 reported); blank.jsonl exits 0 with no error lines.\nFAIL: any other exit code, a missing or extra error line, wrong line number, a blank line reported, the torn last line not reported, or output not in the `<file>:<line>: <error>` form.\n\n### Check 2 — expect: \"A missing file or no argument prints to stderr and exits 2\"\nRun:\n- `node packages/jsonl-lint/bin/jsonl-lint.js $T/does-not-exist.jsonl >$T/o1 2>$T/e1; echo \"exit=$?\"`\n- `node packages/jsonl-lint/bin/jsonl-lint.js >$T/o2 2>$T/e2; echo \"exit=$?\"`\nPASS: both exit 2 and both `$T/e1` and `$T/e2` are non-empty.\nFAIL: either exits with any code other than 2, or its stderr is empty.\n\n### Check 3 — expect: \"packages/jsonl-lint/src/index.js exports lint(text) returning [{ line, error }]\"\nRun from the repo root:\n`node --input-type=module -e 'import { lint } from \"./packages/jsonl-lint/src/index.js\"; console.log(JSON.stringify(lint(\"{\\\"a\\\":1}\\nnope\\n\\n{\\\"b\\\":\")), JSON.stringify(lint(\"{\\\"a\\\":1}\\n\")))'`\nPASS: `lint` is an exported function; the first result is an array of exactly two objects, each having a `line` property and an `error` property, with `line` values 2 and 4; the second result is `[]`.\nFAIL: import fails, `lint` is not a function, the result is not an array, entries lack `line` or `error`, or line values differ.\n\n### Check 4 — expect: \"The workspace has its own package.json (jsonl-lint, type module, test script node --test), no runtime dependencies, and node:test tests for a clean file, a bad middle row, a torn last row, blank lines and the exit codes\"\nRun: `node -e 'const p=require(\"./packages/jsonl-lint/package.json\");console.log(p.name,p.type,JSON.stringify(p.scripts&&p.scripts.test),JSON.stringify(p.dependencies||{}))'`, then `(cd packages/jsonl-lint && npm test)`, and read the test files under `packages/jsonl-lint/`.\nPASS: name is `jsonl-lint`, type is `module`, the test script is `node --test` (it may carry extra arguments such as a test path/glob), `dependencies` is absent or empty; `npm test` in the workspace passes with at least one test run; the test files import from `node:test` and contain tests covering each of: a clean file, a bad middle row, a torn (unterminated) last row, blank lines, and the CLI exit codes (0, 1 and 2).\nFAIL: any field differs, a non-empty `dependencies`, the workspace tests fail or run zero tests, tests not using `node:test`, or any of the five listed cases has no test.\n\n### Check 5 — expect: \"packages/jsonl-lint/README.md exists and the root README lists the tool\"\nRun: `test -s packages/jsonl-lint/README.md && echo ok; grep -n 'jsonl-lint' README.md`\nPASS: `packages/jsonl-lint/README.md` exists and is non-empty, and the root `README.md` mentions `jsonl-lint` as an available tool.\nFAIL: the package README is missing or empty, or the root README does not list jsonl-lint.\n\n### Check 6 — expect: \"The change is one PR on suredesigntshirts/ccp_machine_test whose body says Closes https://github.com/suredesigntshirts/ccp_machine_test/issues/102, and npm test and the test workflow are green at its head\"\nRun: `gh pr list -R suredesigntshirts/ccp_machine_test --state all --search 'issues/102 in:body' --json number,headRefOid,body,state`; `gh pr view <n> -R suredesigntshirts/ccp_machine_test --json body,headRefOid,statusCheckRollup`; `gh run list -R suredesigntshirts/ccp_machine_test --workflow test --commit <headRefOid> --json conclusion,status`; and at the PR head locally `npm ci && npm test` at the repository root.\nPASS: exactly one PR on suredesigntshirts/ccp_machine_test carries this change, its body contains `Closes https://github.com/suredesigntshirts/ccp_machine_test/issues/102`, the `test` workflow run for its head commit has concluded `success`, and local `npm ci && npm test` exits 0 with the jsonl-lint tests running.\nFAIL: no PR or more than one PR for the change, the body lacks that exact Closes line, the test workflow at the head is failing, missing or not completed successfully, or local `npm ci`/`npm test` fails.\n\n## Advisory\n- Also try a CRLF file (`printf '{\"a\":1}\\r\\n{\"b\":2}\\r\\n'`) and running the bin from another cwd; report problems as notes, not failures.\n- Note whether the bin file has a shebang and mode 100755 (`git ls-files -s packages/jsonl-lint/bin/jsonl-lint.js`).\n- A mutation check (e.g. breaking the blank-line skip and seeing a test fail) is a useful signal of test quality but is not a pass/fail condition."}